- Manage their profile.
- Participate in Discover.
- Participate in Community.
- Send and receive messages.
- Manage notifications.
- Report suspicious listings or inappropriate content.

Students must not access landlord, caretaker or administrator management pages.

## B. Property Owner

Property owners can:

- Register as property owners.
- Submit a host application.
- Complete their host profile.
- Submit required verification information.
- Wait for administrator approval.
- Create property listings after approval.
- Upload property images.
- Edit their own properties.
- Manage availability and pricing.
- View enquiries.
- Respond to enquiries.
- Manage viewing requests.
- Communicate with prospective tenants.
- View dashboard statistics.
- Manage their profile.

Property owners must only manage properties they own or are explicitly authorised to manage.

## C. Resident Caretaker

Resident caretakers can:

- Register as resident caretakers.
- Submit a host application.
- Complete their caretaker profile.
- Submit required verification information.
- Wait for administrator approval.
- View properties assigned to them.
- Manage permitted information for assigned properties.
- Upload or manage permitted property images.
- Respond to enquiries for assigned properties.
- Manage viewing requests for assigned properties.
- Communicate with prospective tenants.
- View their caretaker dashboard.

Caretakers must only access properties with an active assignment.

They must never automatically receive access to every property belonging to an owner.

Implement explicit caretaker-to-property assignments.

## D. Administrator

Administrators can:

- Access a protected admin dashboard.
- View platform statistics.
- Manage users.
- Review host applications.
- Approve or reject host applications.
- Review property submissions.
- Approve, reject or suspend listings.
- View reported content.
